{"name":"Collectible","hex":"#9b8467","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"collectible","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Worthy or suitable for collecting on historical/financial grounds, or for meeting a personal aesthetic.","Rightfully subject to payment."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An object which someone might want to collect."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/collectible"}],"entries":[{"title":"Collectable","blocks":[{"text":"A collectable, collectible, or collector's item is any object regarded as being of value or interest to a collector. Collectable items are not necessarily monetarily valuable or uncommon. There are numerous types of collectables and terms to denote those types. An antique is a collectable that is old. A curio is something deemed unique, uncommon, or weird, such as a decorative item. A manufactured collectable is an item made specifically for people to collect."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/World_Expo_88_Collectable_Teaspoons_case_inside.jpg/330px-World_Expo_88_Collectable_Teaspoons_case_inside.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Collectable"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Soviet_Gold_Rings_with_Synthetic_Rubies.JPG/500px-Soviet_Gold_Rings_with_Synthetic_Rubies.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Soviet_Gold_Rings_with_Synthetic_Rubies.JPG/1280px-Soviet_Gold_Rings_with_Synthetic_Rubies.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Soviet_Gold_Rings_with_Synthetic_Rubies.JPG/500px-Soviet_Gold_Rings_with_Synthetic_Rubies.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Collectible Soviet gold rings wi